    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177-a3">

                <pb facs="0392" n="292" xml:id="pg292"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 742.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Prince Kung.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 13,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Informal.]</seg></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of a note from your imperial
                    highness? covering a copy of an edict from His Majesty, directing that the late
                    minister, Chung How, he set at liberty.</p>
                <p>I beg leave to express to your imperial highness the pleasure and satisfaction
                    with which I have learned of this action on the part of His Imperial
                    Majesty.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
